2 CONT Kunigunde [Kunizza] of Diessen, wife of Friedrich I "Roch" (probably count of
2 CONT Diessen, successor of Razzo per De Fundatoribus Monasterii Diessenses); she founded
2 CONT the monasterium sancti Stephani at Diessen in 1020 after her husband's death and was
2 CONT buried there (Diessen necrology: "Chuniza com ... uxor Friderici comes Rochen",
2 CONT ob. Mar Non). Evidence: fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BAVARIAN NOBILITY.htm (married to
2 CONT Friedrich [I] "Roch"; d. 6 Mar after 1020, bur. Diessen St Stefan; De Fundatoribus names
2 CONT "Kunizza comitissa" as wife of "Fridericus comes dictus Roch") +
2 CONT de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Konradiner ("Kunizza († 1020), ⚭ Friedrich I., 1003/1027,
2 CONT Graf wohl von Dießen"). Tree dates kept verbatim (N-5): BIRT Cir 980 and DEAT
2 CONT 6 March 1020 within the literature range; the "(Hemma)" name element is unconfirmed
2 CONT in the literature (no MedLands/Wikipedia attestation of that byname).
