2 CONT Bernard I, King of Italy (Bernardo d'Italia; 797 - 17 Aug 818), son of Pepin of
2 CONT Italy, grandson of Charlemagne; husband of Cunégonde de Gellone (Cunigunde of Laon,
2 CONT @I232222925748@) and father of Pepin I of Vermandois. Blinded after his failed 817
2 CONT revolt against Louis the Pious; died at Milan, buried San Ambrosio/Sant'Ambrogio.
2 CONT Evidence: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernard_of_Italy + fmg.ac MedLands ITALY Kings
2 CONT ("BERNARD ... ([797]-Milan 17 Aug 818, bur Milan, San Ambrosio); m ([813]) CUNIGUNDIS").
